  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 (config_004, acc=0.520) outperforms pca_n2000 (config_001, acc=0.485) as the RNA encoder in singleprofile mode, establishing scvi_n200 as the current best representation. Image-only (resnet50) is very weak (acc=0.208), so the immediate priority is understanding the RNA-side design space before investing in multimodal fusion. Uncertainty: We have no data on whether multiprofile + aggregation adds value over singleprofile. This experiment (config_005: rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) directly extends the best-performing configuration by changing only the profile/aggregation dimension, giving a clean comparison against config_004. If multiprofile+avgpool improves accuracy, it validates the multiprofile axis and justifies further aggregation comparisons (transformer) and multimodal multiprofile tests. If it does not, we can confidently focus budget on singleprofile and encoder/fusion decisions. This is the highest-information next step because the answer gates an entire branch of the configuration space."
}

